"Document", "source_id": "20260627192743196889_bc5542db", "text": "The paper 
\"Some Observations on the Iconography of the ‘Ring of Nestor’\" analyzes the 
imagery on the Ring of Nestor within the broader context of debates about Aegean
forgeries and authenticity. It revisits key iconographic features, including the
depiction of incurved altars, and compares them with other material to assess 
the ring's significance in Minoan and Mycenaean art and its possible 
authenticity. The author emphasizes contradictions or limits in technical 
analyses and argues for the importance of iconographic study in evaluating such 
objects. The paper also notes long-standing scholarly disputes over the 
genuineness of both the Rings of Nestor and Minos and advocates against the a 
priori dismissal of large corpora of unprovenanced or recently discovered rings,
suggesting that such material can be an important resource for understanding 
ancient societies and ring typology."}, {"id": "20260627192743347314_a8442c98", 
